        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_986174655.1",
        "comments": "The assembly lpIsoCern1.hap1.1 is based on 41x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Although the species looks to be diploid, we couldn't distribute the chromosomes between the haplotypes, as the species shows several chromosome rearrangements. Therefore, the entire set of chromosomes is in HAP1 file. The order and orientation of the scaffolds are uncertain: Chromosome 2 from 27.07 to 30.06, Chromosome 4 from 1.73 to 3.19 and on Chromosome 7 from 13.84 to 15.34 Mbp.",
